msgid ""
"[SUPPORTED_IO_MATRIX](https://github.com/tatsuki-"
"washimi/gwexpy/blob/main/SUPPORTED_IO_MATRIX.md)"
msgstr ""
"[SUPPORTED_IO_MATRIX](https://github.com/tatsuki-"
"washimi/gwexpy/blob/main/SUPPORTED_IO_MATRIX.md)"

#: ../../explanation/verification_and_quality.md:13
#: b1b7f998512a4eb0abcc20f9caf6ad45
msgid ""
"Which public format families are tied to which tests and which backends are "
"optional"
msgstr "どの公開 format 群に、どのテストファイルが対応づけられているかと、どこに optional backend があるか"

#: ../../explanation/verification_and_quality.md:13
#: 74ef1855e7bf47b5aaac3befc8e1b383
msgid "Algorithm audit trail"
msgstr "アルゴリズム監査"

#: ../../explanation/verification_and_quality.md:13
#: ../../explanation/verification_and_quality.md:95
#: 3a2574690c8446eea9a41599e7a58f70 84dd0a027bee4626b30fe8f0b1d345c6
msgid "[Validated Algorithms](validated_algorithms.md)"
msgstr "[検証済みアルゴリズム](validated_algorithms.md)"

#: ../../explanation/verification_and_quality.md:13
#: 47c518bf29a543c29b2b514044a8a7c3
msgid ""
"Numerical tolerances, assumptions, and links to audit evidence for selected "
"high-value algorithms"
msgstr "数値許容誤差、前提条件、監査証跡へのリンク"

#: ../../explanation/verification_and_quality.md:13
#: 0450462ed5104a80be0b08377db3eb08
msgid "Repository coverage signal"
msgstr "リポジトリ全体の coverage"

#: ../../explanation/verification_and_quality.md:13
#: 7fa570e288d34376bb8871063819f8ce
msgid ""
"[README codecov badge](https://github.com/tatsuki-washimi/gwexpy) and the "
"linked [Codecov dashboard](https://codecov.io/gh/tatsuki-washimi/gwexpy)"
msgstr ""
"[README の codecov バッジ](https://github.com/tatsuki-washimi/gwexpy) "
"と、そのリンク先である [Codecov ダッシュボード](https://codecov.io/gh/tatsuki-washimi/gwexpy)"

#: ../../explanation/verification_and_quality.md:13
#: 792de8cdbcf946d8b595fc394411d3dc
msgid ""
"Where repository-level line coverage is surfaced publicly, useful as a broad"
" signal rather than a per-feature proof"
msgstr ""
"リポジトリ全体の line coverage がどこで公開されているかを示す入口。feature 単位の証明ではなく、全体傾向のシグナルとして使います"

#: ../../explanation/verification_and_quality.md:29
#: 65d69a54dd7146fa8f8802024f0e800f
msgid "Notebook Validation Policy"
msgstr "Notebook の検証方針"

#: ../../explanation/verification_and_quality.md:31
#: 3b3f36ecc50547258d6c0a657a7e2c3c
msgid ""
"The public notebook policy is defined in the repository's [Notebook "
"Policy](https://github.com/tatsuki-"
"washimi/gwexpy/blob/main/docs/NOTEBOOK_POLICY.md)."
msgstr ""
"公開 notebook の扱いは、リポジトリ内の [Notebook Policy](https://github.com/tatsuki-"
"washimi/gwexpy/blob/main/docs/NOTEBOOK_POLICY.md) に基づきます。"

#: ../../explanation/verification_and_quality.md:33
#: 7bd7540b0431484eb0044c149fc3a412
msgid "The current public model is:"
msgstr "現時点の公開方針は次のとおりです。"

#: ../../explanation/verification_and_quality.md:35
#: c8d822d904ec41f8bec19b30676771b0
msgid ""
"The public [extended verification workflow](https://github.com/tatsuki-"
"washimi/gwexpy/blob/main/.github/workflows/extended-verification.yml) runs "
"cross-platform import smoke tests and the `io-network-backend`, `docs-"
"notebook`, and `io-zarr` gates; it is intentionally scoped to these checks "
"and does not run docstring doctests."
msgstr ""
"公開されている [extended verification workflow](https://github.com/tatsuki-"
"washimi/gwexpy/blob/main/.github/workflows/extended-verification.yml) "
"は、クロスプラットフォームのインポートスモークテストと `io-network-backend`・`docs-notebook`・`io-zarr` "
"ゲートを実行します。意図的にこれらのチェックへ範囲を絞っており、docstring の doctest は実行しません。"

#: ../../explanation/verification_and_quality.md:36
#: 12659c7b95254f9a9d5273377f27daa6
msgid ""
"**Light** notebooks are classified for full execution and validation in CI "
"through `papermill`."
msgstr ""
"**Light** notebook は、Notebook Policy 上では CI で `papermill` により全実行される想定です。"

#: ../../explanation/verification_and_quality.md:37
#: 0bbe54d11f064dafb97fba0e9d1aa85b
msgid ""
"**Heavy** notebooks are kept in CI, but the policy describes them as `nbval "
"--nbval-lax` checks rather than guaranteed full execution."
msgstr ""
"**Heavy** notebook は CI 対象ではありますが、全セル実行を常に保証するものではなく、構造確認や収集確認に寄せて扱われます。"

#: ../../explanation/verification_and_quality.md:38
#: 9ec14c4ef1ad4a36be0b3ad7dfb7d89d
msgid ""
"**Display-only** notebooks prioritize curated outputs and are outside normal"
" execution validation, or limited to load-style checks."
msgstr ""
"**Display-only** notebook は整えた出力の保持を重視しており、「CI で毎回全実行される "
"notebook」と同義ではありません。"

#: ../../explanation/verification_and_quality.md:39
#: 15ee8b3ad3fb4f3a9ab607a21a66efc6
msgid ""
"The public [docs PR workflow](https://github.com/tatsuki-"
"washimi/gwexpy/blob/main/.github/workflows/docs-pr.yml) also executes "
"changed notebooks with `papermill` before building Sphinx HTML."
msgstr ""
"公開されている [docs PR workflow](https://github.com/tatsuki-"
"washimi/gwexpy/blob/main/.github/workflows/docs-pr.yml) では、docs Pull Request"
" で変更された notebook に対して `papermill` が実行されます。"

#: ../../explanation/verification_and_quality.md:40
#: 62ab196bd60d43389a175002463eca89
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Public tutorial notebooks under `docs/web/{en,ja}/user_guide/tutorials/` are"
" treated as the authoritative published copies."
msgstr "公開 notebook のメインのは `docs/web/{en,ja}/user_guide/tutorials/` に置かれます。"

#: ../../explanation/verification_and_quality.md:42
#: 31dcfc9e62d44c7e9a3cd4578ffe4440
msgid ""
"This is why a notebook or docstring example being present in the docs is a "
"useful signal, but not enough on its own to infer that every published "
"sample is executed in every PR, nightly, and release path."
msgstr ""
"したがって、「公開 docs に notebook や例がある」こと自体は有益なシグナルですが、それだけで「あらゆる PR / Nightly / "
"release 経路で毎回一律に実行・保証される」とまでは読まない方が安全です。"

#: ../../explanation/verification_and_quality.md:44
#: 0eca261455db4635b50e437dd802fcec
msgid "Current CI Coverage and Its Limits"
msgstr "現在の CI カバレッジとその限界"

#: ../../explanation/verification_and_quality.md:46
#: 99e4318d3de84541866c454f22707dba
msgid ""
"The current public evidence supports a narrower statement than \"all sample "
"code is universally guaranteed.\""
msgstr "現在の公開根拠から言えるのは、「すべてのサンプルコードが一律に保証される」よりも狭い範囲です。"

#: ../../explanation/verification_and_quality.md:48
#: aba02f4ca6524b1b9ed811d22fed23c8
msgid ""
"The extended verification workflow shows that `gwexpy` runs automated import"
" smoke tests on three platforms plus targeted I/O and docs-notebook gates "
"when the workflow is triggered."
msgstr ""
"extended verification workflow が示すように、`gwexpy` はワークフロー実行時に、3 "
"つのプラットフォームでのインポートスモークテストに加え、I/O と docs ノートブックのゲートを自動実行します。"

#: ../../explanation/verification_and_quality.md:49
#: 77df394431014cb4a3e8a742a20fef75
msgid ""
"The [Notebook Policy](https://github.com/tatsuki-"
"washimi/gwexpy/blob/main/docs/NOTEBOOK_POLICY.md) shows that notebook "
"handling is class-dependent: `Light` notebooks are executed with "
"`papermill`, while `Heavy` notebooks are checked with `nbval --nbval-lax`."
msgstr ""
"[Notebook Policy](https://github.com/tatsuki-"
"washimi/gwexpy/blob/main/docs/NOTEBOOK_POLICY.md) が示すように、notebook "
"の扱いは分類依存で、`Light` は `papermill` で実行、`Heavy` は `nbval --nbval-lax` で確認されます。"

#: ../../explanation/verification_and_quality.md:50
#: 336bf05780594dbc9a6f2389a65722e3
msgid ""
"The docs PR workflow shows that notebooks changed in docs pull requests are "
"executed with `papermill` before the docs build."
msgstr "docs PR workflow では、docs PR で変更された notebook に対して `papermill` が実行されます。"

#: ../../explanation/verification_and_quality.md:52
#: b771d0bb63894073a99287cd10a9be6a
msgid "Read those signals carefully:"
msgstr "このシグナルは次のように読んでください。"

#: ../../explanation/verification_and_quality.md:54
#: 27284982e94a44ddb3843609424ba960
msgid ""
"They show that public examples are not unmanaged; some are exercised "
"automatically in CI today."
msgstr "公開例が完全に放置されているわけではなく、現在も自動検証の経路があります。"

#: ../../explanation/verification_and_quality.md:55
#: 0947f015b9aa4b01ad4fe0ad5e0d55af
msgid ""
"They do **not** mean every published code block is executed in every "
"workflow."
msgstr "ただし、すべての公開コード片が、すべての workflow で毎回実行されることを意味しません。"

#: ../../explanation/verification_and_quality.md:56
#: 9b513f2021ba486295f97510e158997e
msgid ""
"They do **not** mean Doctest or notebook coverage is a single release-"
"blocking gate for the whole documentation set."
msgstr ""
"Doctest や notebook 検証が、ドキュメント全体に対する単一の release-blocking gate だという意味でもありません。"

#: ../../explanation/verification_and_quality.md:57
#: 146ab0fc068749d58985505e842ff90e
msgid ""
"They do **not** remove the need to check notebook class, optional "
"dependencies, and workflow scope before treating an example as strongly "
"guaranteed."
msgstr ""
"強い保証として読む前に、notebook の分類、optional dependency、どの workflow "
"がその対象を見ているかを確認する必要があります。"

#: ../../explanation/verification_and_quality.md:59
#: 06f87b15ef4e42888aa1874f6629bd61
msgid "Direct I/O Verification Visibility"
msgstr "direct I/O の検証可視化"

#: ../../explanation/verification_and_quality.md:61
#: e8b48dad233d4dea8eee53ef26827a79
msgid ""
"The public [SUPPORTED_IO_MATRIX](https://github.com/tatsuki-"
"washimi/gwexpy/blob/main/SUPPORTED_IO_MATRIX.md) is the main visibility "
"layer for direct I/O verification."
msgstr ""
"public direct I/O の検証可視化では、[SUPPORTED_IO_MATRIX](https://github.com/tatsuki-"
"washimi/gwexpy/blob/main/SUPPORTED_IO_MATRIX.md) が主要な入口です。"

#: ../../explanation/verification_and_quality.md:63
#: b1843edb73d94774af6074b7af226855
msgid "Use it when you need to answer questions such as:"
msgstr "この表は、たとえば次のような疑問に答えるときに使います。"

#: ../../explanation/verification_and_quality.md:65
#: 431ea457187142a4a290008098dea4ec
msgid "\"Is this format publicly documented as supported?\""
msgstr "「この format は公開対応としてどこまで見てよいか」"

#: ../../explanation/verification_and_quality.md:66
#: 807475a7760e48b88d9169e096a36fca
msgid "\"Which test file is meant to back this format claim?\""
msgstr "「この format claim はどのテストファイルに紐づいているか」"

#: ../../explanation/verification_and_quality.md:67
#: 609728e0d8e649c28daad49df2dbf0dd
msgid "\"Does this route depend on an optional backend?\""
msgstr "「この経路は optional backend に依存するのか」"

#: ../../explanation/verification_and_quality.md:69
#: 471502284ad247579723c1dd811c3868
msgid ""
"The matrix is especially useful together with the [File I/O Supported "
"Formats Guide](../how-to/io_formats.md):"
msgstr ""
"[ファイル I/O 対応フォーマットガイド](../how-to/io_formats.md) と合わせて読むと、特に役割分担が明確になります："

#: ../../explanation/verification_and_quality.md:71
#: a1622656fd30483e93442bd7c9df5a89
msgid ""
"the user guide explains how to choose and call a public direct-I/O path,"
msgstr "user guide 側は「どう選ぶか」「どう呼ぶか」を説明し、"

#: ../../explanation/verification_and_quality.md:72
#: 773a89d1380a4316a9e45fc88d2cd7b3
msgid "the matrix shows which tests are intended to back that path,"
msgstr "matrix 側は「どのテストが根拠か」を示し、"

#: ../../explanation/verification_and_quality.md:73
#: f1ce9922468645758c4d94d8c79105dc
msgid ""
"and the notes clarify when optional dependencies can cause skips instead of "
"hard failures."
msgstr "備考が optional dependency や skip 条件を補います。"

#: ../../explanation/verification_and_quality.md:75
#: c6e1d8a25e9e40499093bbb45911705f
msgid "Coverage Signals and Their Limits"
msgstr "coverage 表示の読み方と限界"

#: ../../explanation/verification_and_quality.md:77
#: 1245f23f14a74e808362737d3b31eed8
msgid ""
"`gwexpy` publishes a repository-level coverage signal through "
"[Codecov](https://codecov.io/gh/tatsuki-washimi/gwexpy), and the repository "
"[README.md](https://github.com/tatsuki-washimi/gwexpy) surfaces that badge "
"and link publicly."
msgstr ""
"`gwexpy` は [Codecov](https://codecov.io/gh/tatsuki-washimi/gwexpy) "
"によって、リポジトリ全体の coverage シグナルを公開しています。`README.md` にも codecov "
"の状態バッジとリンクがあり、公開された確認入口として辿れます。"

#: ../../explanation/verification_and_quality.md:79
#: 6affedf764444f38a4d94dac6b618e4d
msgid "Read that signal conservatively:"
msgstr "ただし、この値は慎重に読む必要があります。"

#: ../../explanation/verification_and_quality.md:81
#: a5e58b16fb98445b87ce3348940520c4
msgid "it is useful for understanding overall automated test health,"
msgstr "自動テスト全体の健康度をざっくり把握するには有用です。"

#: ../../explanation/verification_and_quality.md:82
#: 6d61aad573f646559f159c174d4414dd
msgid ""
"it does **not** prove that every algorithm branch, notebook, or optional-"
"backend path is equally exercised,"
msgstr ""
"一方で、すべてのアルゴリズム分岐、すべての notebook、すべての optional-backend "
"経路が同じ強さで実行されていることまでは保証しません。"

#: ../../explanation/verification_and_quality.md:83
#: 1041b93d1df146a5bb2e85d2de94442d
msgid ""
"and it should be read alongside page-specific evidence such as the notebook "
"policy, I/O matrix, and audit notes."
msgstr "実際の判断では、Notebook Policy、I/O matrix、アルゴリズム監査ノートと併読してください。"

#: ../../explanation/verification_and_quality.md:85
#: fccf49aa60504eab81ef0ab2c5affa63
msgid "What This Page Does Not Claim"
msgstr "このページが主張しないこと"

#: ../../explanation/verification_and_quality.md:87
#: 0e12b49cc4fa46a2996280e5ee7839d5
msgid ""
"It does **not** claim that every public notebook is fully executed in every "
"CI run."
msgstr "すべての公開 notebook が、すべての CI 実行で全セル再実行されるとは主張しません。"

#: ../../explanation/verification_and_quality.md:88
#: f1398512ae8447dfbc4958bdec4df827
msgid ""
"It does **not** claim that every docstring example or sample code block is "
"executed in every PR, nightly, and release workflow."
msgstr ""
"すべての docstring 例やサンプルコード片が、すべての PR / Nightly / release workflow "
